        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add sub2api provider support",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a native `sub2api` provider backed by its `/v1/usage` endpoint\n- support one labeled group API key per token account, including segmented and stacked multi-account layouts\n- render daily, weekly, and monthly subscription quotas, wallet balance, expiry, and named rate-limit windows\n- document configuration through the app, environment variables, and `config.json`\n\n## Why\n\n[`sub2api`](https://github.com/Wei-Shaw/sub2api) can expose multiple model groups behind separate API keys. CodexBar did not have a provider that could read those group-scoped quotas, so users had to compare the sub2api dashboard manually.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- reads an HTTPS base URL and group API key from provider settings\n- requests `GET /v1/usage?days=30&timezone=<local timezone>` with bearer authentication\n- reconciles daily and Monday-based weekly usage from key-scoped daily usage points, avoiding stale subscription counters\n- applies a strict 15-second total request deadline\n- caches per-account snapshots so segmented switching immediately restores previously fetched groups; uncached selections clear the prior account identity and usage until their refresh completes\n- keeps provider identity, widget registration, CLI diagnostics, configuration validation, icon resources, and documentation in sync\n\n## Review follow-up\n\n- keep account identity and usage aligned by clearing an uncached selection's prior snapshot during the paused refresh state\n- render extra rate-window usage amounts as detail text instead of incorrectly prefixing them with `Resets`\n- reject HTTP 200 usage responses with `isValid: false` as invalid credentials\n\n## Validation\n\n- `swift test --filter 'Sub2APIUsageFetcherTests|Sub2APIMenuCardModelTests|StatusMenuTokenAccountSwitcherTests'` — 22 tests passed across 3 suites\n- `make check` — passed; SwiftFormat reported 0 files requiring formatting and SwiftLint reported 0 violations\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` — passed\n\n### Fresh-bundle live proof\n\nThe freshly packaged `CodexBar.app/Contents/Helpers/CodexBarCLI` fetched three real group API-key accounts from a self-hosted sub2api instance using `--all-accounts`. Names, credentials, identity fields, and the private endpoint are redacted below; quota values are retained to demonstrate distinct group-scoped results.\n\n```text\nGroup A  source=api  exact  daily=$0.00/$120.00  weekly=$0.00/$700.00  monthly=$1,296.23/$2,800.00\nGroup B  source=api  exact  daily=$0.00/$100.00  weekly=$0.14/$700.00  monthly=$0.14/$3,000.00\nGroup C  source=api  exact  daily=$0.00/$50.00   weekly=$0.00/$600.00  monthly=$0.00/$2,500.00\n```\n\nNo credentials, account names, private endpoints, or company data are included in this PR.\n\n## Full-suite note\n\nThe full `make test` run reached existing timing-sensitive `AdaptiveRefreshTimerTests` failures where timer restart/manual-mode cases observed an extra completed refresh. The sub2api and token-account regression suites pass consistently on the current PR head.\n",
