        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: make providers first-class in the docs experience",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add a first-class **Providers** navigation section for the provider reference and all 75 provider guides.\n- Replace the 205-link flat menu with compact disclosure groups that open the current section and expand search matches.\n- Refresh the global docs shell, home page, article typography, light/dark palettes, focus states, and responsive mobile drawer.\n- Add metadata-backed provider filtering for team cloud, managed cloud, sandboxes, GPU/ML, local, self-hosted/BYO, and CI/service providers.\n- Keep wide tables inside keyboard-focusable scroll regions with a sticky first column instead of clipping the page on tablet and mobile.\n- Fix generated markup defects: hidden Markdown comments no longer render, wrapped list items remain valid list children, and active links expose `aria-current`.\n- Reconcile the canonical docs URL and Daytona's current coordinator-supported status across the affected documentation.\n\n## Why\n\nThe generator built every provider page but omitted `docs/providers/**` from `nav`, `sectionByRel`, and `orderedPages`. Provider pages therefore had no sidebar entry, search result, active state, Providers eyebrow, or previous/next navigation.\n\nAdding the missing pages as another flat section would have increased the sidebar from 129 to 205 always-visible links. The provider matrix also forced a 1,042 px document width in a 390 px viewport while `overflow-x: hidden` made its right-hand columns unreachable. This change fixes the information architecture and the responsive layout together.\n\nThis also completes the generated-site navigation part of the provider chooser work tracked in https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/294.\n\n## User impact\n\n- Provider guides are discoverable by browsing or search, including slug searches such as `gcp`.\n- The active docs section stays compact and visible on desktop and mobile.\n- Provider selection can be narrowed by category and free-text capabilities without duplicating the checked provider metadata.\n- Mobile navigation has a backdrop, focus containment, Escape handling, focus return, and inert background content.\n- No configuration or secret changes are required.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- `node --test scripts/check-docs-links.test.js scripts/build-docs-site.test.js`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Playwright layout checks at 1,440 px, 1,024 px, 390 px, and 320 px; root width matched the viewport in every case.\n- Playwright interaction checks for provider filters, mobile menu search, inert state, Escape close, and focus return.\n- Axe scans passed with zero violations on the home page, provider reference, and representative SSH, delegated, local, and service-control provider pages.\n- Rendered light/dark desktop states and the 390 px mobile drawer were visually inspected.\n\n`dist/docs-site` remains generated and is not committed.\n",
